OL,3,GNEWSAI should be dead or in prison -
OL,4,Anow I'm reunited with the teacher who
OL,5,Achanged my life
OL,6,
OL,7,F"Statistically I should be dead, in
OL,8,Fprison or homeless."
OL,10,FSam Gardner lived in 15 foster homes
OL,11,Fbetween the ages of three and 17, and
OL,12,Fsaid the instability was a "big
OL,13,Fchallenge".
OL,15,FHe never felt at home anywhere and was
OL,16,Fsometimes hungry and neglected. When he
OL,17,Fleft the care system at 18, his future
OL,18,Fwas uncertain.
